 # Geometry Shader Voxelization
 
-Also called: GS Voxelization, Solid Triangle Voxelization, Triangle-to-Voxel Rasterization, Triangle Projection Voxelization, OpenGL Geometry Shader Voxelization
+Also called: GS Voxelization, Solid Triangle Voxelization, Triangle-to-Voxel Rasterization, OpenGL Geometry Shader Voxelization
 
 ## Overview
-Geometry Shader Voxelization converts polygonal meshes (`.obj`, `.ply`) into a discrete 3D occupancy or color grid by rasterizing triangles directly into a 3D texture using an OpenGL Geometry Shader [S3, unofficial]. It projects each triangle to cover grid cells at a specified resolution and determines occupied voxels by checking overlaps in all three dimensions (XY, YZ, ZX) [S3, unofficial]. Unlike [GPU Mesh Voxelization via Axis-Aligned Projection](2561-gpu-mesh-voxelization-via-axis-aligned-projection.md) which explicitly selects the optimal projection axis per triangle to maximize coverage, this method swizzles geometry to align with the XY plane while iterating through bounding boxes to verify 3D overlaps [S3, unofficial]. It differs from [GPU Voxelization Using OpenGL Image Atomics](2544-gpu-voxelization-using-opengl-image-atomics.md) by relying on the geometry shader's ability to emit multiple primitives and iterate through grid cells, rather than pure atomic accumulation without depth-based projection [S3, unofficial].
+Geometry Shader Voxelization converts polygonal meshes (`.obj`, `.ply`) into a discrete 3D occupancy grid by rasterizing triangles directly into a 3D texture using an OpenGL Geometry Shader [S3, unofficial]. It determines occupied voxels by projecting triangles onto axis-aligned planes, computing edge distances, and iterating through the triangle's bounding box to check for overlaps in all three dimensions (XY, YZ, ZX) [S3, unofficial]. Unlike [A-Buffer Solid Voxelization](1189-a-buffer-solid-voxelization.md) which uses a 2D accumulation buffer to resolve depth, this method explicitly tests 3D spatial overlap per voxel index within the shader loop, ensuring watertightness without traditional framebuffer depth buffers [S3, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:**
-- Mesh vertices $V$ (3xN floats) and faces $F$ (3xM uint32s) loaded from `.obj` or `.ply` files [S3, unofficial].
-- Voxel resolution `dim` (e.g., 64), applied uniformly to x, y, z axes [S3, unofficial].
-- Thickness mode: `THIN` (0) or `FAT` (1) [S3, unofficial].
-
-**Outputs:**
-- Occupancy Grid: A 3D texture (`GL_TEXTURE_3D`) with internal format `GL_R8UI` (8-bit unsigned integer, single channel) [S3, unofficial].
-- Voxel Color: A 3D image `voxelColor` with format `rgba8` storing color data [S3, unofficial].
+**Inputs and Outputs:**
+*   **Input:** A triangle mesh defined by vertex positions $V$ (size $3 \times N$) and face indices $F$ (size $3 \times M$) [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Output:** A 3D occupancy grid (texture) where occupied voxels are marked with a flag (e.g., 1) and optionally color data [S3, unofficial].
 
 **Data Structures:**
-- `mesh.V`: Eigen matrix, size 3xN, float [S3, unofficial].
-- `mesh.F`: Eigen matrix, size 3xM, uint32 [S3, unofficial].
-- `voxelResolution`: Uniform `ivec3` [S3, unofficial].
-- `unswizzle`: Permutation matrix to reverse coordinate transformation [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Voxel Resolution:** A cubic grid dimension `dim` (e.g., 64), applied uniformly to x, y, z axes [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Occupancy Grid:** A 3D texture (`GL_TEXTURE_3D`) with internal format `GL_R8UI` (8-bit unsigned integer, single channel) [S3, unofficial]. Dimensions are `voxelResolution[0] x voxelResolution[1] x voxelResolution[2]` [S3, unofficial]. Bound as an image buffer `id_image_occupancy` at binding point 0 with access `GL_READ_WRITE` [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Color Buffer (Optional):** A 3D image `voxelColor` with format `rgba8` storing color data [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Unswizzle LUT:** A lookup table storing permutation matrices to reverse coordinate transformations applied during dominant axis alignment [S3, unofficial].
+
+**Parameters:**
+*   `voxelResolution`: Uniform `ivec3` specifying grid dimensions [S3, unofficial].
+*   `THICKNESS`: Compile-time constant (`0` for Thin, `1` for Fat) selecting the voxelization style [S3, unofficial].
 
